ing Harden ahead, or if Democratic outside spending materializes late, this race could move toward the tossup column.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert rater lists this race; treated as safe for the party holding the seat.", "Open seat: Barry Loudermilk (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Barry Loudermilk's retirement opened Georgia's 11th District, a northwest Atlanta suburban seat with a Republican lean of about twelve points. John Cowan won a contested GOP primary in June and enters the general election with a decisive financial advantage, having raised roughly $2.3 million and drawn over half a million dollars in outside support, while Democrat Chris Harden has raised under $100,000 with minimal outside help.\n\nA single September poll of likely voters showed Harden narrowly ahead, but it carries little weight on its own and conflicts with the district's fundamentals. Prediction markets give Harden only about a three percent chance. The race remains Likely Republican, with Cowan favored by roughly nine points, though the open-seat nature of the contest leaves somewhat more uncertainty than a typical incumbent-held year.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1084, "margin": -8.05}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0743, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0742, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1332, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1182, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1179, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1154, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1025, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1012, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1158, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0772, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0621, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.16, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0837, "margin": -9.0}]}